............................ [ 71%]\n........................................................................ [ 85%]\n....................................................s................... [100%]\n503 passed, 1 skipped, 39 deselected in 16.82s\n","tested_git_commit":"4b5c6411f27642d3be2da4ce27d064eefbb95ec9"},"source_path":".superpowers/sdd/2026-10-27-cgoc/task-12-final-verification.json","source_sha256":"6850d6ce0e1d875b221d14b4f176c4a63cf3ec42867bcfc6a0c36a5225863533"},"task-12-inherited-prerequisites.json":{"content":{"checks":[{"path":"provenance/teacher-qualification-2026-10-27.json","reviewed_commit":"346f241","same_bytes":true,"sha256":"6e3c5958c62e013a9136cbf616876f542e5701086789082af22d15016c557e1a"},{"path":"provenance/payload-anchor-135m.json","reviewed_commit":"1b7d075","same_bytes":true,"sha256":"8b9b9c38ee9f1f1116ba3ab897c678cd039e952907b326a4c3b6b4f4eb48f46e"},{"path":"poc/data/access.py","reviewed_commit":"066ad5d","same_bytes":true,"sha256":"bd7ac16cc3d5ef70b6388d70724f19f6c8072cbd3c416fa4ca264ce2da6cd634"},{"path":"poc/data/manifest.py","reviewed_commit":"066ad5d","same_bytes":true,"sha256":"be12ccb04aef2d8109176a84246c3de26f7bdce317b8f238cbafd2c4e3f9386f"},{"path":"poc/runtime/torch_decoder.py","reviewed_commit":"066ad5d","same_bytes":true,"sha256":"726458296828b23e30cd6cabdd7b7ac98c618deea82ffbe6c6255b139c894dee"}],"scope":"No deployment/capability requalification claimed by Task12; prior Tasks6–11 reviewed; no new source/asset/runtime numerical changes through diagnostic; native run receipts validate actual declared execution.","status":"resolved_inherited_unchanged_evidence"},"source_path":".superpowers/sdd/2026-10-27-cgoc/task-12-inherited-prerequisites.json","source_sha256":"7eb7c0d64a385ee491c5f6a5f97b37d8eeddd1ddbb4b5a8a87e7339c3d1b7300"},"task-12-review.md":{"content":"### Spec Compliance\n\n- ✅ Spec compliant for the controlled single-merge diagnostic and justified terminal WP04 INCONCLUSIVE. The required implementation, tests, pilot configuration, protocol and progress changes are present. Common medoid inputs and fitted identities are enforced in `poc/merge.py:66`, `poc/merge.py:126` and `poc/diagnostics.py:119`; candidate selection and sampled oracle are recomputed in component resamples at `poc/diagnostics.py:132`. R25 explicitly permits a diagnosed inconclusive WP04 (`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-cgoc-design.md:320`, `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-cgoc-design.md:328`), matching the evidence-limited decision and Task25 routing at `provenance/task12-wp04-2026-10-27.json:99` and `provenance/task12-wp04-2026-10-27.json:133`.\n- ⚠️ Historical teacher/MPS qualification, prepared-data leakage protections and the immutable native payload anchor are inherited prerequisites, not independently requalified by this diff. The controller should preserve their existing receipts and protected-data seals through Task25; this diagnostic provides no new native deployment or capability qualification (`protocol/development.md:229`, `provenance/task12-wp04-2026-10-27.json:100`).\n\n### Strengths\n\n- Both parent medoids see identical fit records; deterministic selection preserves unaffected groups. Fitting rejects a previously fitted trial and requires its complete common allowance. Compact restoration verifies base, teacher, weight-file and final fitted identities (`poc/merge.py:66`, `poc/merge.py:126`, `poc/merge.py:154`, `poc/merge.py:168`; behavioral fixtures in `tests/test_merge_trials.py:24` and `tests/test_merge_trials.py:77`).\n- Frozen edits are reused while boundaries are rebuilt for the actual fitted candidate. Teacher suffix execution preserves the prefix producer identity. Conditional intervention scores remain distinct from natural complete-model KL; no cross-candidate hidden-state cache is introduced (`provenance/measure_single_merge.py:166`, `provenance/measure_single_merge.py:201`).\n- The pure scoring layer rejects empty, nonfinite, misordered or mismatched populations and score/damage component overlap. Bootstrap draws move whole source-component vectors across all pairs and methods, reselecting candidates and the damage oracle; discrete choice counts and both signs of contrast are retained (`poc/diagnostics.py:91`, `poc/diagnostics.py:119`, `poc/diagnostics.py:132`, `provenance/summarize_single_merge.py:13`).\n- Original20, original18 secondary, fresh16/32 and pooled24/48 secondary analyses remain separate. Fresh eligibility follows a frozen reserve order and persists short/rejected cases; exact reconstruction is checked before fresh predictions, without adding learning to primary states (`provenance/measure_single_merge_precision.py:184`, `provenance/measure_single_merge_precision.py:225`, `provenance/measure_single_merge_precision.py:298`, `provenance/measure_single_merge_precision.py:339`, `provenance/measure_single_merge_precision.py:376`).\n- Costs preserve the logging-only failed profile, the failed 8 GiB preparation, all 18 reconstructions and separately charged CPU diagnoses. Later caps are versioned, and exact uncached disk accounting retains file-symlink, hidden-file, broken-link and directory-symlink semantics with mutation/overrun tests (`provenance/measure_single_merge.py:29`, `provenance/measure_single_merge_precision.py:43`, `provenance/measure_single_merge_precision.py:50`, `provenance/measure_single_merge_precision.py:105`, `tests/test_precision_replay.py:94`). Shared pool costs are explicitly distinguished from efficient method-specific acquisition costs (`provenance/measure_single_merge.py:386`, `provenance/summarize_single_merge_precision.py:54`).\n- Scientific scope is appropriately narrow: only 20/435 pairs and 2/23 shortlist members; one-update learning remains sensitive to another step; raw SVD is permutation-sensitive; all functional point choices agree within each analysis but change across original/fresh data. These support diagnosed uncertainty, not equivalence, active superiority, universal absence of reuse or a pretrained joint-composition claim (`poc/diagnostics.py:188`, `poc/merge.py:138`, `provenance/measure_single_merge_sensitivity.py:21`, `provenance/task12-wp04-2026-10-27.json:133`).\n\n### Issues\n\n#### Critical (Must Fix)\n\n- None identified.\n\n#### Important (Should Fix)\n\n- None identified.\n\n#### Minor (Nice to Have)\n\n- `PROGRESS.md:3` and `PROGRESS.md:8`: the opening “Current restart index” still says the precision follow-up is pending and directs the next worker to resolve reconstruction. Both are already complete, and `PROGRESS.md:35` correctly routes to Task25 after review. Update the opening summary and next-action bullet during Task25 finalization so a reader does not mistake historical work for an outstanding instruction. The authoritative terminal gate and explicit later entry make this a documentation inconsistency, not a defect in the measured result.\n\n### Checks and Evidence Limits\n\n- Reviewed the supplied base-to-head package (`066ad5d9530fd43b5ecd8ca0f5f8b7e002cb59d1` → `9a13b70136dcd1550b4519ab0fae73064440e80c`), all implementation/test hunks, amendments, gate and receipt structures. Large receipt hash maps and repetitive masks were inspected through bounded structured reductions; initially truncated output was recovered in smaller or compacted portions. No git commands, model jobs or test suite reruns were performed.\n- Named boundary/SVD risk: inspected only the relevant unchanged helpers, confirming CPU FP64 SVD work in `poc/bank.py:44`, producer checks in `poc/probes.py:272`, conditional teacher branches in `poc/probes.py:306`, and executor-versus-producer semantics in `poc/runtime/torch_decoder.py:295`. These support the new callers without relabeling candidate boundaries as teacher boundaries.\n- Named terminal-routing risk: checked R25/WP04 directly at `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-cgoc-design.md:320`. Diagnosed inconclusive completion is expressly allowed; remaining uncertainty is not being turned into a precise negative finding.\n- Named provenance/privacy/accounting risks: inspected public receipt fields and serializers at `provenance/summarize_single_merge.py:33` and `provenance/summarize_single_merge_precision.py:18`; the three public single-merge receipts contain no raw text/token payload keys. Read the provided independent controller final and statistics evidence: 92 fresh artifact references, 352 source bodies, 323121 fresh cost rows, preserved failed memory peak, independent seven-method point reductions and retained-draw summaries. Those audits verify recorded evidence, not independent neural replication (`.superpowers/sdd/2026-10-27-cgoc/task-12-controller-final-evidence.json:1`, `.superpowers/sdd/2026-10-27-cgoc/task-12-controller-statistics-evidence.json:1`).\n- Existing final verification is 503 passed, 1 explicit-assets skip, 39 hardware deselections, exit 0 in 16.82 seconds. The supplied record explicitly identifies its stdout as a transcription of retained tool output and binds 102 code/test/config files from tested HEAD to review HEAD (`.superpowers/sdd/2026-10-27-cgoc/task-12-final-verification.json:1`). The recorded final stdout has no warning. The separately recorded inherited macOS Torch redirect notice remains a deferred minor item; this review found no new output concern. No unresolved doubt required an additional test.\n\n### Assessment\n\n**Task quality:** Approved.\n\n**Reasoning:** The controlled comparison, component-level uncertainty, exact-state reuse and failure-preserving resource accounting support the restricted WP04 INCONCLUSIVE result. Proceed to Task25 after recording this review, carrying the minor restart-index correction; the evidence does not justify compiler continuation or stronger scientific claims.\n","source_path":".superpowers/sdd/2026-10-27-cgoc/task-12-review.md","source_sha256":"6e3b04a1fb2c9f42d65f7cea67f7d45b4fbedebbe2b06e36fef7495314ccbb32"}},"review_status":"Approved","schema_version":1,"scope":"Preserved controller audits/review, not ind